### Search operators

Parse the query for explicit search operators. These are hard constraints the user typed deliberately. They are not optional concepts.

- Exact-phrase: any span inside double quotes "..." must appear VERBATIM in the snippet (the content between `<<<SNIPPET>>>` and `<<</SNIPPET>>>`) or the document title (case-insensitive, whitespace-normalized; ignore surrounding punctuation). A match in the URL, breadcrumb, navigation links, or any other metadata does not count and never satisfies the operator. Do not assume or infer presence: locate the exact span in the snippet or title, or treat it as missing. Each quoted span is a separate required string.
- site:domain = the document URL host must equal or be a subdomain of `domain`.

If the query has no operators, skip operator gates and score normally.

